                        <p><span data-field="contents.strengthening_communities">{{ contents.strengthening_communities }}</span> . . . <span data-field="contents.page_7">{{ contents.page_7 }}</span></p>
                        <p><span data-field="contents.conferences_symposiums">{{ contents.conferences_symposiums }}</span> . . . <span data-field="contents.page_8">{{ contents.page_8 }}</span></p>
                        <p><span data-field="contents.a_national_model">{{ contents.a_national_model }}</span> . . . <span data-field="contents.page_9">{{ contents.page_9 }}</span></p>
                        <p><span data-field="contents.pathway_forward">{{ contents.pathway_forward }}</span> . . . <span data-field="contents.page_10">{{ contents.page_10 }}</span></p>
                        <p><span data-field="contents.the_equity_imperative">{{ contents.the_equity_imperative }}</span> . . . <span data-field="contents.page_11">{{ contents.page_11 }}</span></p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div style="width: 55%;">
                    <div style="border-left: 3px solid #a03030; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 20px; margin-top: 0;">Message from the President</h3>
                        <p style="font-size: 14px;">As I begin another year as president, I am encouraged by the accomplishments of our professors, students and staff in helping to build the resilient, sustainable, and equitable university that the District of Columbia needs. But our work has just begun.</p>
                        <p style="font-size: 14px;">When we started three years ago, our battle cry was "equity." Today, we are building a university that is equitable, and our challenge was reversing the trend of declining graduation rates. We have been working on the core of this institution. Mayor Muriel Bowser answered the call, providing millions in additional funds to grow programs and update infrastructure—a down payment on the type of ongoing commitment that is required to build a modern public university.</p>
                        <p style="font-size: 14px;">We have hired dozens of new faculty, earned commendations from our accreditors, cleaned up our books, and laid the groundwork to show our community that the University of the District of Columbia is the kind of value-added partner that the city and its residents deserve.</p>
                        <p style="font-size: 14px;">We are making strides in the classroom, in research, and in community-based learning, and touching lives across our campus—the District of Columbia. One example is the Capital Builders Center, a public-private</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
        <div style="width: 30%;">
            <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 0;">UDC: Key to a Resilient, Sustainable, and Equitable District</h3>
                <p style="font-size: 14px;">UDC has developed an overarching strategy that will transform it into the critical resource the community of the District deserves.</p>
                <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-around; margin-top: 20px;">
                    <div style="text-align: center;">
                        <div style="font-size: 36px; font-weight: bold; color: #a03030;">92%</div>
                        <p style="font-size: 12px;">of Whites</p>
                    </div>
                    <div style="text-align: center;">
                        <div style="font-size: 36px; font-weight: bold; color: #a03030;">25.6%</div>
                        <p style="font-size: 12px;">of Americans</p>
                    </div>
                    <div style="text-align: center;">
                        <div style="font-size: 36px; font-weight: bold; color: #a03030;">41.5%</div>
                        <p style="font-size: 12px;">of Latinos</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p style="font-size: 12px; text-align: center; margin-top: 15px;">D.C. Residents with College Degrees</p>
            </div>
            <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 15px;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 0;">Median Salaries in D.C.</h3>
                <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-around;">
                    <div style="text-align: center;">
                        <div style="font-size: 24px; font-weight: bold;">$65,886</div>
                        <p style="font-size: 12px;">Bachelor's Degree</p>
                    </div>
                    <div style="text-align: center;">
                        <div style="font-size: 24px; font-weight: bold;">$30,311</div>
                        <p style="font-size: 12px;">High School Diploma</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 70%;">
            <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
                <div style="width: 48%;">
                    <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 15px;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 0;">Closing the Gap</h3>
                        <p style="font-size: 14px;">Educational equity is the pathway to national security and stable communities. The Equity Imperative is about closing gaps and building a pathway to the middle class for D.C. public school students from economically disadvantaged families.</p>
                        <p style="font-size: 14px;">Many obstacles challenge UDC's efforts: insufficient resources, aging technologies, and inadequate infrastructure. UDC has developed an overarching strategy that will transform it into the critical resource the community of the District deserves.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div style="width: 48%;">
                    <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 15px;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 0;">UDC is a hidden community treasure that empowers all District residents with learning opportunities to build a better future.</h3>
                        <p style="font-size: 14px; margin-top: 15px;">–Phil Mendelson, Chairman, Council of the District of Columbia</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
        <div style="width: 30%;">
            <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 0;">Laying the Foundation</h3>
                <p style="font-size: 14px;">UDC's growth as a university is defined through the accomplishments of our faculty, workforce, and students. Whether in the form of professional certification or academic degrees, our colleges, schools and workforce development units are making strides in the classroom, in research, and in community-based learning.</p>
                <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-around; margin-top: 20px;">
                    <div style="text-align: center;">
                        <div style="font-size: 24px; font-weight: bold;">152</div>
                        <p style="font-size: 12px;">Workforce Development Students</p>
                        <p style="font-size: 10px;">Transitioned into Full Degree Programs in 2016</p>
                    </div>
                    <div style="text-align: center;">
                        <div style="font-size: 24px; font-weight: bold;">Over 300</div>
                        <p style="font-size: 12px;">DC-UP Students</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 15px;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 0;">Memberships:</h3>
                <ul style="font-size: 14px; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li>Federal City Council,</li>
                    <li>D.C. Chamber of Commerce</li>
                </ul>
                <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 20px;">Two New PhD Programs</h3>
                <p style="font-size: 14px;">Faculty and Staff</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 70%;">
            <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
                <div style="width: 48%;">
                    <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 15px;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 0;">MSCHE Accreditation</h3>
                        <p style="font-size: 14px;">Accreditation until 2024</p>
                    </div>
                    <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 15px; margin-top: 20px;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 0;">New LEED Platinum Certified Student Center</h3>
                        <p style="font-size: 14px;">Becoming a modern public urban system of higher learning requires ongoing research into solutions specific to urban challenges. The community we serve, we make progress every day toward our goal of being a model for the nation.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div style="width: 48%;">
                    <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 15px;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 0;">National Accreditations</h3>
                        <ul style="font-size: 14px; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li>University accredited by MSCHE through 2024 (with 11 commendations)</li>
                            <li>Program Accreditations:</li>
                            <li>B.S. in Nutrition and Dietetics program accredited by ACEN through 2022</li>
                            <li>Environmental Quality Testing Laboratory accredited by NELAP through 2019</li>
                            <li>R.N. in B.S. program accredited by ACEN through 2023</li>
                            <li>Programs in the School of Engineering and Computer Science accredited by ABET through 2020</li>
                            <li>University's Bachelor's Degree Programs in Civil, Electrical, and Mechanical Engineering accredited by ABET through 2021</li>
                            <li>Computer Science Degree Program accredited by ABET through 2020</li>
                            <li>Master of Architecture Program Granted Three-Year Accreditation by NAAB through 2020</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 15px; margin-top: 20px;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 0;">Firsts</h3>
                        <ul style="font-size: 14px; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li>First PhD Program (Engineering and Computer Science)</li>
                            <li>One of the first schools in the Nation to implement a Faculty Electronic Portfolio Submission Process</li>
                            <li>Online Graduate Degree in Urban Sustainability (Professional Science Master's Degree-PSM)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
        <div style="width: 30%;">
            <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 0;">Building Credibility</h3>
                <p style="font-size: 14px;">UDC's Board of Trustees is a diverse group of professionals with experience in education, government, military, healthcare, and law. New management includes the President and Heads of the Community College, Student Success, Human Resources, Legal Affairs, Finance, and University Police. Ninety-seven highly qualified new faculty members hired.</p>
            </div>
            <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 15px;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 0;">Accomplishments in Leadership</h3>
                <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
                    <div style="width: 48%;">
                        <p style="font-size: 14px;">Forty Faculty Awarded the Distinguished Teaching Credential (DTC)</p>
                        <p style="font-size: 12px;">Recognized Teaching Credential</p>
                    </div>
                    <div style="width: 48%;">
                        <p style="font-size: 14px;">Winners of 2017 John & Suanne Rouche Excellence Awards.</p>
                        <p style="font-size: 12px;">Recent Faculty Publications</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
                    <p style="font-size: 12px;">• Amanda Huron authored Caring Out the Commons: Tenant Organizing and Housing Cooperatives in Washington, D.C.</p>
                    <p style="font-size: 12px;">• Anika Burton, Jeffrey Fleming and Pamela Henderson published "Landscapes Through Public Higher Education."</p>
                    <p style="font-size: 12px;">• Professor Judith Kower authored a chapter in DC: Stories of Jazz Music in Washington, D.C.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 70%;">
            <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
                <div style="width: 48%;">
                    <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 15px;">
                        <h3 style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 0;">New Research and Grants</h3>
                        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 15px;">
                            <div style="width: 48%;">
                                <h4 style="font-size: 14px; margin-top: 0;">National Science Foundation</h4>
                                <p style="font-size: 12px;">Broadening Participation Research Project</p>
                                <p style="font-size: 12px;">Investigating the impact of Mentoring on STEM Retention and Persistence Among Minority Undergraduate Women</p>
                                <p style="font-size: 12px;">Dr. Julian Weber, $266,178 (No)</p>
                            </div>
                            <div style="width: 48%;">
                                <h4 style="font-size: 14px; margin-top: 0;">National Institute of Technology</h4>
                                <p style="font-size: 12px;">A $6.76 million project that will involve faculty members, students, and undergraduate and graduate students in research and interdisciplinary projects.</p>
                                <p style="font-size: 12px;">Dr. Kate Klein</p>
                            </div>
